# mossferry servers declaration — TSV, not YAML.
# Locations (later wins per port):
#   1. ~/.config/mossferry/servers.tsv
#   2. <repo>/.ferry/servers.tsv  (under FERRY_REPO_BASE)
#
# Columns (tab-separated):
#   port	id	class	label	mac	health
#
# class: spine|docker|dev|preview|db|agent|infra
# mac:   ok|prefer-ts|never
# health: URL or -
#
# Declarations never assert liveness — they contribute label, class, and mac
# policy only. A live ss reading always wins on bind and pid. A declared port
# with no listener becomes state declared-missing.
#
# Blank lines and # lines are skipped. Unknown extra columns are ignored.
# "-" means "not set".
#
# Why TSV, not YAML/JSON: mossferry is zero-dependency bash. yq and jq are not
# required; parse with: while IFS=$'\t' read -r port id class label mac health

# port	id	class	label	mac	health
8791	freellmapi	infra	FreeLLMAPI	never	http://127.0.0.1:8791/health
3000	syndcast-next	dev	Syndcast app	ok	-
3100	syndcast-render	dev	Syndcast render	ok	http://127.0.0.1:3100/health
5432	postgres	db	Postgres	never	-
